{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on whether a lottery contains a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability). In the decision problem, Lottery A has two outcomes: -1000 Euros with 50% probability and 0 Euros with 50% probability — thus, no sure outcome. Lottery B has -500 Euros with 100% probability — this is a sure outcome. Therefore, the reason can be applied: Lottery A lacks a sure outcome, while Lottery B has one. The decision reason prefers the lottery without a sure outcome, which is Lottery A.",
